WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.650
This is... my favorite place...

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.160
No one ever stops by this remote corner.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.240
I see... So this is where you battle, Hitoe-san?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.170
N-No. I also got my cards only recently...

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:29.460
The battle against Akira-san was...
m-my very first battle.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:36.840
I've been practicing different battle simulations in my mind while Midoriko taught me how to play.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.430
Like these...

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.100
Wow!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.270
Please don't look at it so closely!

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.190
But I still wasn't prepared for...

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.360
Real battles are different after all.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.110
I don't think I was ready for one yet...

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.580
Then why do you want to battle me?

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.410
W-Well...

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.500
You looked weak, so I thought I'd do fine against you...

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.960
You're pretty blunt, huh?

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:14.590
I-I'm sorry! B-But I really want to win...

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>She's really trying her best.</i>

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:28.770
<i>If she can win this battle and
get closer to her wish, then...</i>

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.570
Let's battle.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.710
Open!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:14.440
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.950
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.700
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.710
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.960
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:38.010
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.260
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:46.350
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:51.650
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:57.400
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.490
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:07.830
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:14.040
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.800
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.600
Yay! I'm battling with Yuzu-pon! I'm battling with Yuzu-pon!

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.610
I go first!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.200
Draw! Enercharge! I summon Amethyst!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:51.290
<i>If she uses that Peeping-something move, I'm gonna be in trouble.</i>

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.380
With Amethyst's power, I banish Refraize and attack with Sapphire!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>I'll lay it on now before she
even gets to use that move!</i>

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.720
Hanayo-san, Attack!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.720
Ouchy! You're <i>so</i> aggressive! Shame on you!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.310
It's my turn now. Piruluk-tan, Grow.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.190
And now for a Spell! It's bye-bye time for your card!

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.150
Too Bad!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.150
Here it comes...

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.610
And I'll have you toss away... let's see... that one!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.750
Aww... A level 1 card? Weak.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:35.040
So you're the type to prefer attacking with tons of weak cards, right?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.590
It's my choice how I battle!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.460
I was just giving you some advice...

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.300
Running a red deck doesn't mean you <i>have</i> to be super-straightforward, you know?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.050
<i>Your battle style is way too straightforward, Yuzuki.</i>

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.430
What's so wrong with being straightforward?!

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.480
Open!

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:12.200
The field feels a lot warmer compared to the time I battled Akira-san...

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.120
You're right.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.210
It's different from when I battled Yuzuki-san, too.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.830
This wind feels nice!

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.460
The affinity between Selectors manifests in a field.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.420
Affinity?

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.550
Hitoe, you're green,
and Ruuko is white... a fairly rare color.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.600
It's almost as if sunlight is filtering through trees.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.020
I see...

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:39.060
I feel this battle will be more relaxing, Midoriko!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.520
Let's do our best!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.820
Hitoe-san and Midoriko-san are both really nice.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.910
Ruuko-san, please go first!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.000
Um, sure.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.870
Well then, Draw... and Enercharge. Tama, Grow!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.300
I don't have any level 1 cards... Turn End.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.880
I won't lose!

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:08.300
Draw 2, Enercharge! I summon Mike and Mike!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.060
Mike, Attack!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:25.650
<i>This is totally different from
my games at home with Grandma.</i>

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:31.570
<i>My ears are burning up... I can actually feel the pain...</i>

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.490
But...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.290
I can feel my heart beating, too!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.420
Tama, Grow to level 2!

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.000
I summon Round and Square!

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.670
Attack Mike with Round. Banish it!

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.710
Attack with Square!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.340
She's coming, Midoriko-san!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.720
Tama, Attack!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.930
A-Again?! Midoriko!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.360
Midoriko-san!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.860
I'm fine... Let's Grow!

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:11.780
Okay!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.700
Midoriko-san, level 2! I summon Shiro!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.660
Midoriko Arts. Giant!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.920
Shiro gains +5000 power until the next turn!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.500
Shiro, Attack!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.510
I shouldn't win...

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.220
Ruuko-san?

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.640
It looks like she lost her spirit all of a sudden.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.390
Now's your chance, Hitoe! Attack!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.100
Y-Yes!

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.860
After all, I...

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.490
Tama!

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.780
Piruluk-tan, Grow!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.700
She has enough Ener...

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.250
Arts. Peeping Analyze.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.000
It's coming now.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:10.800
That move... it won't <i>only</i> discard my cards...

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.550
<i>Let me guess why you want to be an Eternal Girl....</i>

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.930
She'll see it... she'll find it out...

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.350
There's nothing wrong with that!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.810
Hanayo-san...

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.480
Everyone will find it out anyway if your wish comes true.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.520
Just brace yourself.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:29.650
Knowing her, she'll use
that knowledge to harrass you,

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.570
but your wish is nothing to be ashamed of!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.410
Right!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.080
Let's toss out your level 1 cards!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.750
And now... I'll take a peek into your wish.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.080
Piruluk-tan, look into her!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.470
Immoral.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.390
She loves her younger brother.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.510
Wh-What?! No way!

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.520
That was her younger brother?!
The pipsqueak with the same face?!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.520
Calm down.
That was her younger brother?!
The pipsqueak with the same face?!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.690
I know... I know...

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.570
No way! No way! Just, <i>no way</i>!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.110
How lewd! That's just <i>too</i> pervy!

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:12.690
Sh-Shut up...
How lewd! That's just <i>too</i> pervy!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.320
That's <i>super</i> immoral!
Sh-Shut up...

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.410
I know a word for this.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.950
Want me to spell it out for you?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.040
I-N-C-E—

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.290
Shut up!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.040
Shut up! Shut up! <i>Shut up</i>!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.920
Yuzuki!

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.960
Dominating Fury!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:37.590
Don't do it! If you use such a burdening Arts now...!

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.800
Stop! Yuzuki!

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:49.730
<i>If I win, Hitoe-san's wish won't come true.</i>

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.070
<i>That's right...</i>

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.020
No!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.110
I want to win... so, no!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.620
Tama? You just... talked?!

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:02.540
No... losing on purpose.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:06.460
No. I want to win. Tama wants to win!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.420
Tama!

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.830
"On purpose"?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.170
You were planning to lose on purpose, Ruuko-san?!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.920
I wouldn't be happy to win that way!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:16.970
There'd be no meaning to it!

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:18.800
Hitoe-san?

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.680
There's no use for me to hide it anymore...

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.140
I have no friends.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.440
I moved from Aomori to Tokyo.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:36.530
I had an accent and was indecisive,
so I couldn't make any friends...

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.490
<b>Uemura
But then I got a letter from my friend in Aomori.</b>

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:42.280
But then I got a letter from my friend in Aomori.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.870
I read it over and over again, and it saved me.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.460
To me, a friend is a very beautiful thing!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:54.840
Hitoe-san...

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:58.880
And that's why I don't want to
taint my wish with cheating!

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:03.140
I want to do my best, and I want to make my wish come true the right way!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.350
You're really cool, Hitoe-san.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:10.850
I'm sorry.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:16.280
I don't even have a wish, but I still
want to battle with all my might!

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.820
That's right, I'll battle with all I've got!

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.450
Ruuko-san!

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.780
Good! We'll give it all <i>we've</i> got, too!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.700
Yes!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.920
<i>This is fun!</i>

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.290
Tama!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:37.000
<i>I feel the excitement swelling inside me... so much it makes me want to shout!</i>

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.050
Spell. Oversize! All SIGNIs gain Power!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.010
I won't let that spell be used!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.510
Anti-Spell!

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.680
<i>This is the first time I've felt this good!</i>

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.100
Midoriko!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.730
I'm fine.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:56.400
Hitoe...

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.570
You did well.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.070
I...

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.030
won?

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:13.500
A real battle feels... <i>amazing</i>.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:22.510
Huh? The battle is over, but we
haven't been sent back to our world?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:26.300
I wonder what's going on, Tama.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.560
Tama?

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.400
Tama?!

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.320
Tama?!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:46.950
Tama!

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.630
She evolved.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:01.550
Evolved? That's different from the Grow action?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:10.140
The closer a Selector gets to becoming
an Eternal Girl, the more we LRIGs gain power.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.640
Wow, Tama! You're beautiful!

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.640
Ruu, thank you!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.480
Tama! You're speak—

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.540
Tama?

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:36.460
She's in the same new state even in her card form.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:41.340
You're right. It looks like the
words here have changed, too.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.760
Um, Ruuko-san? Tama?

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.510
I'm sorry I said that you looked weak!

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.680
You were both very strong.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.640
Hitoe-san.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:57.390
If I lose one more time, my wish won't come true.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.860
But I won't regret it!

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.650
Actually, I may regret it a bit...

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.690
Um...

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:04.400
Yes?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:08.430
Putting all this Eternal Girl stuff aside, I was thinking we could become friends,

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.030
if you're all right with that...

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.830
Wh-What?!

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.870
You know, I also just moved here,
and I couldn't make any friends at first either.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.750
But it felt really good when I finally did make a friend.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:27.550
So I thought—wait, no, maybe you don't want this, but if you do...

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.550
N-Not like?! No! I...

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.470
Excuse me...

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.560
Could you be a little more quiet down there?

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.520
S-Sorry!
S-Sorry!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:40.230
Um, I... I'll think about it!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.190
Hitoe-san...

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.110
She's already asleep.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:57.450
Wow, it's so dark already.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.540
Grandma's probably worried.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.150
My, a book about the card game?

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:10.380
<b>Bookstore
WIXOSS Card Encyclopedia
My, a book about the card game?</b>

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.850
This is quite something.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.520
Each card is carefully explained in detail.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.060
Yeah, it has a lot of cards I've never seen...

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.730
Hey, this one looks pretty good!

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:24.820
What are you doing?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:31.950
You know, I met this girl today, and she had all kinds of notes on the decks and the battle flow.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.740
Do you think you can be friends?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.330
Well, I'm waiting for her answer.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:46.920
Coming, coming... You'll let me
take a look after dinner, right?

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.840
We can battle then, too!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:57.260
<i>With how Tama is now, I can add more red cards and work them with Search effects.</i>

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.270
<i>This just might work!</i>

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:04.350
<i>But if I swap out some cards, my deck will become weaker compared to Yuzuki-san's pure red deck...</i>

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:09.110
<i>It's fun, so I'll keep battling.
That's reason enough for now.</i>

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>And if that's okay, then I...</i>

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.740
Incoming

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.200
I'll get it!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.290
Hello!

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.910
Huh? Kazuki-kun? What's the matter?

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:26.340
Yuzuki-san?!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.880
Yuzuki-san hasn't come home yet?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.050
Can you get in touch with her?

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.050
She hasn't phoned or emailed me back yet.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:40.680
I thought she might be at your house.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.640
Maybe...

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.600
Akira-san?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.450
<i>What's the matter?</i>

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.380
Don't tell me you overdid yourself!

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.960
You totally went too far.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.920
Oh well, it's about time I turn the tables.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.300
Here I come!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:23.140
<i>If only I had Adamasphere to counter with, like Kazuki told me to get...</i>

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.940
All right, Piruluk-tan! Finish them!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.490
Hanayo-san!

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.830
I'm sorry, Hanayo-san.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.000
Yuzuki!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.540
Yuzuki-san!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.630
Did you battle Akira?!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:58.180
Wait! Why'd you battle her?!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.010
Let me go!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:02.310
I told you that you can't beat her with what you've got now! Why did you—

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.220
Shut up!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.100
Yuzuki...

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.020
You'd never understand, Kazuki...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.560
You'd never understand how I feel!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.780
Yuzuki...

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:19.240
That's...

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:23.490
I was talking to Momoka-san,
and I got this for you.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.540
Is that why you met Momoka-san today?

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:29.920
How did you know?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:37.380
Momoka-san said she had a customer
willing to trade it, so she put us in touch.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:40.760
Why...

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.390
Shining Battle Stone Adamasphere
Why...

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.220
Why didn't you just tell me?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:49.270
I didn't want you to get your hopes up prematurely, just in case the trade didn't work out.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.400
I'm sorry I was so harsh on you, Yuzuki.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.610
I mean, you've only just
started playing after all, right?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.150
Kazuki...

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.490
This card will make you stronger, Yuzuki.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:01.570
This is only the beginning.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:05.080
I'll keep helping you, so let's get better together, okay?

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:10.670
Yuzuki—

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.500
I'll be fine!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.880
Just leave me alone for a bit...

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.590
I'm sorry!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.090
Yuzuki...

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:24.140
Kazuki-kun... Yuzuki-san must be really important to you.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.470
She is.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:30.100
I was really weak and shy when I was a kid.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.100
Yuzuki was always there to help me.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.400
But now it's my turn.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:38.070
I want to do my best to help Yuzuki make her wish come true.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.410
And when Yuzuki's wish comes true,

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.870
I can finally say that I was able to help her.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:54.130
<i>Stupid Kazuki... Why are you so nice to me?</i>

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:01.550
<i>It just hurts when you're like this...</i>

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.890
Good morning!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.270
Akira, you're late! Hurry and get ready!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.810
I'm sorry!

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.020
Looking good, Iona!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.810
Yeah, nice and cute!

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.280
Excuse me...

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.320
Fuck this!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:29.080
I've beaten Hitoe, and I've beaten Yuzuki...

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.910
So why isn't anything changing?!

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:35.790
If you lose three WIXOSS battles,
you lose the right to enter battles!

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.750
Just how many times do you have to win to become an Eternal Girl?!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.260
Winning alone is not enough to become an Eternal Girl.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:45.970
Every wish has its own specific
conditions that need to be met.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.510
Spill it, then.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.770
Do it, or I'll rip you up...

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:59.070
Come now, better tell me before it's too late.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.980
You ready?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.570
Then tear me apart.

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:08.120
The hell! You're pissing me off, you and your tone!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:12.410
The way you're talking... it reminds me of her...

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:17.750
Iona... It's only a matter of time until I stick that grand face of yours into the dirt.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.960
Just you wait...

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:29.970
Hey, Iona. It smells like Akira was in a battle. She has the scent of victory.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:32.600
She seemed pretty upset, though.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.850
Hey, Iona! Let's just get rid of Akira.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:41.570
I'm sure seeing her cry will feel amazing. It'll be such a spectacle.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.490
Stop saying such brutish things. Or else I'll burn you.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:48.490
My, how scary...

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.960
This
Peace
is
Nonsensical

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:28.050
It doesn't bother me one bit.

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:29.470
Orihalcum, Attack!

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:32.050
I wonder what it feels like to be in love.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:34.600
That feels so weird...

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:36.970
WIXOSS is so... wonderful.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:37.310
That
Wish
is
Blasphemy

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:39.930
That wish is blasphemy.
That
Wish
